WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.680
Idea. After a night studying until late, you feel foggy and slow at school. After a good night's sleep you feel sharp. Sleep is not wasted time. Your body and brain are busy while you sleep.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:27.776
Sleep is not one state. It moves in sleep cycles. One cycle lasts about ninety minutes, and it repeats four or five times a night. Each cycle has four stages of non-REM sleep, then REM sleep.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:44.519
REM stands for rapid eye movement. In REM the eyes dart about and the brain is very active. The heart rate rises. But the body muscles are paralysed, so the body does not move. Most vivid dreaming happens in REM.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:01:00.371
Why does sleep matter? Deep sleep releases growth hormone, which repairs the body. Sleep saves energy. It helps the brain consolidate memories, which means store them firmly. And it keeps attention, concentration and mood steady.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:06.485
The question asks you to state a stage or a benefit, then link it to the person in the story.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:24.932
Method. Step one: state the stage feature or benefit accurately. That earns the first mark. Step two: link it to the person or what they did in the scenario. That earns the second mark. The trap is a vague answer, such as sleep is good for you, with no link.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:35.745
For stage questions, match the clue to the stage. Spindles mean stage two. Delta waves mean stages three and four. Darting eyes mean REM.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:53.262
Worked example. Here is a real two mark question. Aditi has a nurse interview in three days. She will do decision-making activities and a test on medication, patient care and her legal duties. We explain one benefit of sleep that may help her.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:02:01.019
Aditi has a test on facts. So choose the benefit that fits. Sleep helps the brain consolidate memory.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:11.071
Mark one is the benefit. Sleep helps the brain consolidate memories, so things learnt in the day are stored more securely and are easier to recall.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:18.688
Mark two is the link. This helps Aditi remember medication, patient care and her legal duties in the test.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:28.603
A tempting wrong route is to say sleep is good for your health, so she will do well. That is too vague. It names no benefit and does not use her interview.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:47.421
Here is the answer. Sleep helps the brain consolidate memories, so learning is stored and easier to recall. This helps Aditi remember medication, patient care and her legal duties in the test. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:59.128
Common mistake. The classic slip is saying the body moves a lot in REM. It does not. In REM the eyes dart, but the body muscles are paralysed.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:17.375
Your turn. Now you try. Izzy is doing a sleep study. A participant shows eye movements about ninety minutes after falling asleep. Izzy thinks they could be dreaming. Explain why, referring to REM sleep. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:37.829
Answer. Eye movements show the participant may be in REM sleep, which stands for rapid eye movement. About ninety minutes is the end of the first cycle, when REM can begin. The brain is very active in REM, and most vivid dreaming happens there. So Izzy thinks they could be dreaming.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:47.561
The common wrong answer says the eye movements show the participant is awake, or in deep sleep. But in deep sleep the eyes are still. Name REM.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.247
So state the feature. Link it to the person. Say why it matters.
